    "description": "The PG1202SA is here because it is what many shoppers find when they search for a 1,200-watt generator, and we would rather explain it than leave it out. It is rated at 1,200 peak and 900 running watts from a two-stroke engine, which means mixing two-stroke oil into every tank of fuel. It is a conventional generator, not an inverter, so its power is not as clean as the others here; we would not run a laptop, a CPAP or a modern TV from it. Retailers list it at about 35 pounds with a tank of about 1.1 gallons and a listed 5 hours at half load, and a retailer Q&A notes that it is generally not recommended for a full-size refrigerator. For lights and simple tools, it works. For anything else, spend the extra on the WEN."
