          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What will a 1500 watt generator run?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A 1,500-watt generator typically runs at about 1,000 to 1,200 watts, which covers a full-size refrigerator, LED lights, phones, laptops, a router, a TV and a CPAP. It can run a small coffee maker or a 5,000 BTU window AC on its own. It will not run a microwave, space heater on high, hair dryer or well pump.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a 1500 watt generator run a refrigerator?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Usually yes. A typical full-size refrigerator runs at 100 to 200 watts with a startup surge several times higher, and the 1,250 to 1,500-watt surge ratings in this class handle most modern fridges. Large side-by-sides and older units can be harder to start, so check the label or measure with a plug-in watt meter.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a 1500 watt generator run a space heater?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not a standard 1,500-watt heater on high. That draws 12.5 amps continuously, above the running rating of every generator in this class. A heater with a 750-watt low setting will run on a 1,000 to 1,200-watt unit, but runtime falls to a few hours and nothing else can share the power.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between a 1200 and a 1500 watt generator?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Usually about 100 to 300 running watts. A 1,200-watt unit typically runs at 900 to 1,000 watts; a 1,500-watt unit at 1,000 to 1,200. The extra matters for starting a refrigerator alongside other loads or running a small window AC. Compare running watts, not the peak number on the box.
