            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long will a 1500 watt generator run on a tank?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It depends on the load. Westinghouse rates the iGen1500c at up to 12 hours at quarter load on 0.79 gallons. The Honda EU1000i is rated at 7.1 hours at quarter load and 3.2 at rated load. The WEN 56125i and Pulsar PG1500iS are listed at about 5 hours at half load.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you parallel two 1500 watt generators?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Some, yes. Westinghouse lists the iGen1500c as parallel capable, and the WEN 56125i manual shows parallel ports. Two 1,000-watt running units give roughly 2,000 running watts together. Use two identical units and the manufacturer's parallel kit, which is often sold separately. Not every small generator supports parallel, so check before buying.
              </p>
            </div>

