          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people the Westinghouse iGen1500c is the right 1,500-watt generator: 1,000 clean running watts, a rated 12 hours at quarter load, a CO shutoff sensor and parallel capability, for considerably less than the Honda. If you need the extra 200 running watts and can live with more noise and less runtime, the Pulsar PG1500iS is the stronger engine; if price is everything, the WEN 56125i is the cheapest good inverter.
          </p>
